){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/281"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Épée, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2167"} "Grand Palais, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2011087"} "35 from 19 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/151928"} "Máté Koch"] " was the 2023 World Champion, was world ranked #1, and was the #1 seed in Paris. He had a bye in round one, and then, in a huge upset, lost to Venezuela’s 32nd seed, " [:a {:href "/athletes/151987"} "Grabiel Lugo"] ", 15-10."] "\n\n" [:p {} "That left the competition wide-open with no clear favorite. The second seed was another Hungarian, " [:a {:href "/athletes/143678"} "Gergely Siklósi"] ", but he went out in round three, losing to Belgium’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/151870"} "Neisser Loyola"] ". By the quarter-finals, only two of the top eight seeds remained – Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144612"} "Koki Kano"] " (#4) and France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/122240"} "Yannick Borel"] " (#3)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kano and Borel made their way to the final, where Kano won an unlikely gold easily, 15-9. Kano had no previous international medals individually except in local Asian competition. Borel had been World Champion in the individual épée but that was back in 2018."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bronze medal match came down to the 10th seed, Egypt’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502902"} "Mohamed El-Sayed"] " defeating another Hungarian, " [:a {:href "/athletes/151929"} "Tibor Andrásfi"] ", the 16th seed. El-Sayed’s bronze medal was only the second by an Egyptian in Olympic fencing, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/123357"} "Alaaeldin Abouelkassem"] " had won silver in the 2012 men’s individual foil."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144612"} "Koki Kano"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122240"} "Yannick Borel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "10"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2502902"} "Mohamed El-Sayed"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/EGY"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/EGY.png"}] "EGY"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "16"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151929"} "Tibor Andrásfi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151936"} "Federico Vismara"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td 